  "helpTitle": "How to play",
  "helpBody": "Each round shows a 4-digit number. Keep the digits in order and fill the slots under the spaces between them with symbols so that both sides of the = sign have the same value.\n\nExample: 5261 becomes (5 − 2)! = 6 × 1.\n\nClick a slot, then click symbols (or drag them in). Click a placed symbol to remove it. Digits with nothing between them join into a bigger number.\n\nLevels: Easy allows fractions, ⌊x⌋ and ⌈x⌉. All other levels only allow exact integer divisions. Intermediate drops ⌊ ⌋ ⌈ ⌉, Advanced also drops ∛ and **, and Hard also drops √ and !.\n\nHints (the 3 hearts): 1 shows where the = goes, 2 shows which symbols are used, 3 fills in the solution. Using 1 or 2 hints halves the points; revealing the solution gives 0.\n\nKeyboard: type + - * / ( ) | ! = , ^ for **, R for √, C for ∛, arrows pick a slot, Backspace deletes, Esc clears, Enter checks, H hint, S skip.\n\nToo hard? Press SKIP to get another number.",
